  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK Aid Match Fund III: Climate Resilient Agriculture (Caritas Switzerland)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is part of a consortium based programme in which 5 organisations are collaborating together to support poor women, men and children from hazard-prone or marginalised rural communities to adapt their livelihoods strategies to better cope with climate-related shocks and stresses. Caritas Switzerland will provide technical support in the districts of Dinajpur and Rajshahi for the implementation and use of solar powered irrigation pumps. Caritas Switzerland will organise the purchase of 30 solar pumps from the Solar Pump Association Switzerland and be responsible, jointly with Caritas Bangladesh, the import and install the pumps in small-holder farmer fields. Caritas Switzerland will be responsible to monitor the effectiveness and impact of the pumps and organise any required adjustments or maintenance during the life of the programme.</narrative>
  </description>
